# ripgrep-only (not git): re-include what .gitignore hides but agent Grep/Glob must still
# reach. Nested .gitignore files sit deeper and still win, so each sub-repo prunes its own
# junk (AvatarProject/Library/, PackageCache/).
!/AvatarProject/
!/vrc-unity-tools/
!/vrc-blender-tools/
!/vrc-skills/
!/vrc-bridge/
!/vrc-patterns/
!/vrc-mcp-proxy/

# Local scratch: dispatch board, coordinator state, briefs, specs. Agent-authored, so
# agent-searchable — the governed-prose fence excludes it separately, by path.
!/docs/local/

# Left hidden on purpose, not drift — each swamps or pollutes a workspace-wide grep, and each
# is still readable by explicit path: /references/* (third-party clones, some license-encumbered;
# README.md is un-ignored in .gitignore and stays greppable as their pointer), /Sandbox/
# (measured 11.7k files even with Library/ pruned — 13x the rest of the workspace; AvatarProject
# is the sandbox agents search), /showcases/ (media + raw transcripts), /test-output/ and
# /TestEditor*/ (disposable, regenerated).
